Grammar:

Rule 0     S' -> program
Rule 1     program -> func_def
Rule 2     func_def -> INT ID LPAREN RPAREN LBRACE decl_stmt_list stmt_list RBRACE
Rule 3     decl_stmt_list -> empty
Rule 4     decl_stmt_list -> decl_stmt_list decl
Rule 5     stmt_list -> empty
Rule 6     stmt_list -> stmt_list stmt
Rule 7     empty -> <empty>
Rule 8     decl -> STRING id_list SEMICOLON
Rule 9     decl -> CHAR id_list SEMICOLON
Rule 10    decl -> DOUBLE id_list SEMICOLON
Rule 11    decl -> INT id_list SEMICOLON
Rule 12    id_list -> ID
Rule 13    id_list -> id_list COMMA ID
Rule 14    stmt -> print_stmt
Rule 15    stmt -> assign
Rule 16    assign -> ID ASSIGN expr SEMICOLON
Rule 17    print_stmt -> PRINT expr SEMICOLON
Rule 18    expr -> expr QUESTION expr COLON expr  [precedence=right, level=1]
Rule 19    expr -> LPAREN INT RPAREN expr  [precedence=right, level=5]
Rule 20    expr -> LPAREN DOUBLE RPAREN expr  [precedence=right, level=5]
Rule 21    expr -> expr NE expr  [precedence=left, level=2]
Rule 22    expr -> expr EQ expr  [precedence=left, level=2]
Rule 23    expr -> expr GE expr  [precedence=left, level=2]
Rule 24    expr -> expr LE expr  [precedence=left, level=2]
Rule 25    expr -> expr GT expr  [precedence=left, level=2]
Rule 26    expr -> expr LT expr  [precedence=left, level=2]
Rule 27    expr -> STRING_CONST
Rule 28    expr -> CHAR_CONST
Rule 29    expr -> REAL_CONST
Rule 30    expr -> LPAREN expr RPAREN
Rule 31    expr -> expr REMAINDER expr
Rule 32    expr -> expr DIVIDE expr  [precedence=left, level=4]
Rule 33    expr -> expr TIMES expr  [precedence=left, level=4]
Rule 34    expr -> expr MINUS expr  [precedence=left, level=3]
Rule 35    expr -> expr PLUS expr  [precedence=left, level=3]
Rule 36    expr -> ID
Rule 37    expr -> NUMBER

Terminals, with rules where they appear:

ASSIGN               : 16
